00:09:55.485 --> 00:10:03.105
$10,000 in cash and three account doors, TFSA, RRSP, and FHSA, and walking through the

00:10:03.105 --> 00:10:06.945
wrong door first can leave thousands in lost tax savings over a decade.

00:10:07.565 --> 00:10:09.685
Motley Fool Canada lays out the mechanics.

00:10:09.685 --> 00:10:13.425
The TFSA grows tax-free with no tax on withdrawal.

00:10:14.065 --> 00:10:18.605
The RRSP delivers an immediate tax refund, but taxes withdrawals as income.

00:10:19.285 --> 00:10:23.225
And the FHSA combines both benefits only for first-time home buyers.

00:10:23.845 --> 00:10:29.525
The correct order depends on current marginal tax rate, expected future tax rate, and whether

00:10:29.525 --> 00:10:31.265
home ownership is a near-term goal.

00:10:31.845 --> 00:10:35.305
Contribution room in a TFSA carries forward indefinitely.

00:10:36.065 --> 00:10:42.005
RRSP room resets each year based on earned income, and FHSA room is caped at a lifetime

00:10:42.005 --> 00:10:48.285
limit of $40,000. A higher current tax rate favors the RRSP for the immediate deduction,

00:10:48.765 --> 00:10:54.285
whereas a lower expected future rate favors the TFSA for tax-free growth. The practical

00:10:54.285 --> 00:11:00.325
sequence begins with the FHSA if a home purchase is planned within 15 years, then the TFSA

00:11:00.325 --> 00:11:03.785
for flexibility, then the RRSP for the tax refund.

00:11:04.485 --> 00:11:10.465
Modeling a $10,000 contribution at a 40 percent marginal rate shows an immediate $4,000 refund

00:11:10.465 --> 00:11:17.505
in the RRSP versus zero in the TFSA, yet the TFSA preserves full access without clawback

00:11:17.505 --> 00:11:19.325
on future income-tested benefits.

00:11:20.045 --> 00:11:25.905
The TFSA offers the most flexibility for any future need, while the RRSP provides the largest

00:11:25.905 --> 00:11:31.585
up front tax saving when income is high, dividend payers such as Scotiabank fit inside any of

00:11:31.585 --> 00:11:36.685
these accounts, but the tax credit on eligible Canadian dividends provides an extra advantage

00:11:36.685 --> 00:11:43.285
only in non-registered accounts. FHSA contributions can be transferred tax-free to an RRSP

00:11:43.285 --> 00:11:48.945
if home purchase plans change, so the choice hinges on whether you value immediate tax relief,

00:11:49.605 --> 00:11:55.565
long-term tax-free growth, or the specific home buying incentive. Run the after-tax outcome with your

00:11:55.565 --> 00:12:00.585
own bracket and current room before the transfer, because sequencing errors compound over

00:12:00.585 --> 00:12:01.005
decades.

